06 00:00:00','MM/DD/YYYY HH24:MI:SS'),null,'PIV11-W-41503',to_date('03/15/2010 00:00:00','MM/DD/YYYY HH24:MI:SS'),'26926',to_date('02/27/2009 00:00:00','MM/DD/YYYY HH24:MI:SS'),'Y',null,'n/a',null,null,null,null,to_date('01/03/2008 00:00:00','MM/DD/YYYY HH24:MI:SS'),null,'4132 Napali Place','Honolulu','HI','96816',null,'Marc Nadon','NADON MARC 536873','Y',null,null,null,'MNADON',null,null,null,null,null,null,'Canada','Canada',null,null,'Honolulu','HI','J','JIMAR, CRED',to_date('03/17/2007 00:00:00','MM/DD/YYYY HH24:MI:SS'),to_date('03/14/2008 00:00:00','MM/DD/YYYY HH24:MI:SS'),'Ferguson, Scott','(808) 983-3736','PIFSC Kewalo Research Facility','Canada',null,'Mr. Nadon is a Marine Ecosystems Specialist working for the University of Hawaii?s Joint Institute of Marine and Atmospheric Research.  His primary responsibility in that position is to assist NOAA in the collection and processing of mapping and monitoring data that documents the state of the coral reef ecosystems throughout the U.S.-affiliated Pacific Islands.  He has expertise in reef fish behavioral ecology with over 500 hours of diving associated with underwater research and excellent knowledge of Indo-Pacific reef fish taxonomy.   Mr. Nadon?s primary workplace is at the Pacific Islands Fisheries Science Center?s Kewalo Research Facility, however, he routinely sails onboard the NOAA Ships HI?IALAKAI and OSCAR .E. SETTE.  Mr. Nadon?s specialized knowledge and extensive field experience benefits NOAA by helping to ensure the timely production of coral reef ecosystem monitoring reports.  During his work at KRF and aboard the NOAA ships, Mr. Nadon has access to the public spaces of the work places and research vessels and is treated as member of the scientific party.  During his work Mr. Nadon does not have access to sensitive information or access to controlled technologies.',null,null,null,null,'Marc is working at the University of Miami.',null,null,null,to_date('09/15/2011 12:35:23','MM/DD/YYYY HH24:MI:SS'),'RAKI');
